skill: "fundraising-data-room"
sections[3]:
  - "# fundraising-data-room\n\nAssemble and police the diligence data room: the index of required documents, the chase list for missing items, redaction rules and the access policy. Use when a raise starts, when investor diligence begins, or before any data room link is shared, so access is deliberate and the index is complete.\n\nOwner: role-cfo (pod-gna, executive). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"diligence index template data-room-template.toon; corporate registry; financial artifacts (cashflow-13w.toon, cap-table-scenarios.toon, settlement-recon.toon); legal artifacts from role-general-counsel and role-ip-patent-attorney\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/data-room-index.toon with sections[], item status, owner and redaction flags; access-policy block; completeness report\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Instantiate data-room-template.toon as the index; every item records its section, source artifact or owner, status and redaction flag.\n2. Map each index item to an existing AGYOS artifact where one exists; items with no source become the chase list with a named owner and a due date.\n3. Apply redaction rules per item class: employee identifiers, customer names and security specifics are redacted by default; each redaction states the rule that required it.\n4. Define the access policy: tiered access (summary financials, full financials, legal), who grants access, and the log requirement for every grant.\n5. Verify completeness with run_command against the index: an incomplete room is reported with the exact open items, never released as ready.\n6. Emit ask_question to role-cfo for tier grants above the summary tier and for any redaction exception.\n7. Record every access grant and its approver in the index's access-log[]; grants without approver entries are defects.\n8. On raise close, archive the index and access log with the round reference; diligence artifacts outlive the deal and get reused in the next one.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ngrants via role-cfo; legal items sourced from role-general-counsel and role-ip-patent-attorney.\n"
